# Shell scripts MUST be LF. They are executed on Linux (the EC2 deploy box and
# inside Docker), where a trailing CR makes bash fail with an opaque
# "syntax error: unexpected end of file". Windows checkouts default to CRLF via
# core.autocrlf, so without this any .sh copied straight from a Windows working
# tree to the server is silently broken.
*.sh text eol=lf
# Workflow `run:` blocks are bash executed on Linux runners and hit the exact
# same CRLF trap: a trailing backslash before a CR escapes the CR, so every
# line continuation splits into separate commands and the step half-runs.
.github/workflows/*.yml text eol=lf
.github/workflows/*.yaml text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.pem -text
